[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi!<br>\nI built a macro that appends a list of user defined args to a list of predefined args and generates a <code>simp [...]</code> call with all the args.<br>\nI think I messed up some of the separators or something, because at call site it generates an unsupportedSyntax exception.<br>\nHow can I have a look at the syntax objects involved in my macro definition?<br>\nI parse around \"TSepArray\"s and \"Array (Syntax `term)\" and I think it would be really helpful to have a look at them, but I can't figure out how.</p>",
        "id": 598415877,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1779999049
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In other monads I'd point you to <code>trace[debug]</code>, but in <code>MacroM</code> take a look at the more low-level <code>dbg_trace</code> :) Depending on what's failing to match and whether you're using <code>macro_rules</code> or not, though, you might not even have the chance to run that code. Would you mind sharing some more explicit code?</p>",
        "id": 598419203,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1780000344
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I just figured out that I could do <code>#eval myMacro [...]</code> and use <code>dbg_trace</code> to debug the values. Thanks!</p>",
        "id": 598419321,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780000402
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I just couldn't get it to output anything when deploying the macro inside a proof.</p>",
        "id": 598419388,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780000424
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'll try my best and post the code If I don't get any further.</p>",
        "id": 598419448,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780000450
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Okay, actually, my code was completely wrong <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span>.<br>\nI'd like to have the following:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">baseSimpArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TSepArray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"ss\">`simpErase</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`simpLemma</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\",\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">doSmthSimilarToSimpAllToObtainTSepArray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">thm1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">thm2</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">thm3</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"n\">thm4</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Can I somehow use the existing parser for <code>simp_all [...]</code> for this?</p>",
        "id": 598422199,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780001660
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have this syntax def:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"custom_simp_all\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"only\"</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"[\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">simpErase</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simpLemma</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"]\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 598422376,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780001734
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This gives me the list of args the user supplied. I now want to prepend some other theorems before the supplied ones.</p>",
        "id": 598422533,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780001811
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, I see. This is genuinely a little awkward if you try to construct everything before inlining it, I think :) But does doing something direct like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">macro_rules</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">custom_simp_all</span><span class=\"bp\">%$</span><span class=\"n\">tk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"bp\">%$</span><span class=\"n\">onlyTk</span><span class=\"o\">]?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">]]?)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getD</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∅</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp_all</span><span class=\"bp\">%$</span><span class=\"n\">tk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"bp\">%$</span><span class=\"n\">onlyTk</span><span class=\"o\">]?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">baz</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">bat</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>work for you? Then we bypass manipulating <code>TSepArray</code>s directly :)</p>",
        "id": 598425956,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1780003290
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ahh, very nice. I couldn't figure out the % stuff. I think your version will work, but I just wanted to point out that doing</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">baseArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">dsimpArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">thm1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">thm2</span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n<span class=\"n\">baseArgs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>gives you at least something to start working with, when going the MacroM way.</p>",
        "id": 598426320,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780003443
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I didn't know that executing parsers worked like that.</p>",
        "id": 598426449,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780003505
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Indeed! We do lose all the nice syntax typing there, unfortunately, but it's good to be aware of it as an escape hatch to typed syntax. :)</p>",
        "id": 598426570,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1780003563
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh yeah, and by the way, if you haven't seen it before, the <code>%$stx</code> stuff is a way of getting/attaching position information from/to tokens like <code>simp_all</code> (so it can affect where errors get logged). And in the <code>only%$onlyTk</code> case it serves another role: since <code>onlyTk</code> is bound within <code>$[]?</code>, it's an <code>Option _</code>, and behaves as you'd hope within a subsequent <code>$[]?</code>. That is, the resulting <code>only</code> token will be constructed only if <code>onlyTk</code> is <code>some _</code>.</p>",
        "id": 598426960,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1780003744
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Does the % stuff also work for defining syntax?</p>\n<p>Currently I have the following:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"custom_simp\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"only\"</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">dsimpArgs</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"custom_simp?\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"only\"</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">dsimpArgs</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 598426977,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780003752
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It should work in any quotations <del>regardless of whether you've defined it or not</del> (oops misread, I don't think this is what you were asking) :) All that's necessary is that <code>%$foo</code> follows an actual token. It won't work when attached to complex syntax constructions. (Beware, <code>(...)%$tk</code> \"works\", and associates <code>tk</code> to the syntax of the <code>)</code>!)</p>",
        "id": 598427474,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1780003980
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, I just had a look at the syntax definition of <code>simp</code>/<code>simp_all</code> and  they also have two syntax defs. One for the normal version and one for the trace version.</p>",
        "id": 598427713,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780004110
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm not totally sure what you meant when asking whether it works for defining syntax; do you mean in a <code>syntax</code> command?</p>",
        "id": 598427730,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1780004123
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I was unsure why I couldn't do <code>syntax \"custom_simp\" \"?\" ...</code> (or something with %) instead of having two different syntax defs.</p>",
        "id": 598427853,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780004175
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But I guess that's just because of the way tokens are parsed.</p>",
        "id": 598427883,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780004191
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah I see, yeah; exactly, something like <code>\"custom_simp_all\" (noWs \"?\")?</code> won't get the chance to parse the way you hope.</p>",
        "id": 598428038,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1780004258
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh, I just noticed that the <code>custom_simp?</code> versions fail with \"Tactic <code>tacticCustom_simp?Only_</code> has not been implemented\"</p>",
        "id": 598428143,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780004303
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Some tactics use</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"tac\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"?\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"tac?\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and then have a macro turning <code>tac?</code> into <code>tac ?</code> to reduce code duplication <span aria-label=\"grinning face with smiling eyes\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f601\" role=\"img\" title=\"grinning face with smiling eyes\">:grinning_face_with_smiling_eyes:</span></p>",
        "id": 598428153,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1780004309
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1030095\">Jannis</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Debug.20macro.20generating.20unsupportedSyntax.20exception/near/598428143\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Oh, I just noticed that the <code>custom_simp?</code> versions fail with \"Tactic <code>tacticCustom_simp?Only_</code> has not been implemented\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Ah, then there's probably a case you haven't given macro_ or elab_rules to yet. :)</p>",
        "id": 598428275,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1780004357
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Do you have an idea why this fails?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"custom_simp\"</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"s2\">\"only\"</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">dsimpArgs</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"custom_simp?\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"only\"</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">dsimpArgs</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">macro_rules</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">custom_simp</span><span class=\"bp\">%$</span><span class=\"n\">tk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"bp\">%$</span><span class=\"n\">onlyTk</span><span class=\"o\">]?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">]]?)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getD</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∅</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp_all</span><span class=\"bp\">%$</span><span class=\"n\">tk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"bp\">%$</span><span class=\"n\">onlyTk</span><span class=\"o\">]?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">custom_simp?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I thought the % would have defined this case.</p>",
        "id": 598428604,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780004523
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, no, the match against <code>custom_simp%$tk</code> is the same as a match against <code>custom_simp</code>. It just binds the variable <code>tk</code> to the syntax <code>custom_simp</code>.</p>",
        "id": 598428676,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1780004567
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So currently there are no cases that would match <code>custom_simp?</code>.</p>",
        "id": 598428716,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1780004595
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ahh, that makes total sense.</p>",
        "id": 598428762,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780004618
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But why would I bind it at all in this example then? For only I somehow need to.</p>",
        "id": 598428823,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780004644
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But for the first not necessarily (it works without)</p>",
        "id": 598428859,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780004665
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This also leads me to my original pain point:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">macro_rules</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">custom_simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"bp\">%$</span><span class=\"n\">onlyTk</span><span class=\"o\">]?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">]]?)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getD</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∅</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp_all</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"bp\">%$</span><span class=\"n\">onlyTk</span><span class=\"o\">]?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">large</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">thms</span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">custom_simp?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"bp\">%$</span><span class=\"n\">onlyTk</span><span class=\"o\">]?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">]]?)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getD</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∅</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp_all?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"bp\">%$</span><span class=\"n\">onlyTk</span><span class=\"o\">]?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">large</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">thms</span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>has a lot of code duplication...</p>",
        "id": 598429032,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780004754
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That's why I wanted to have a function that concatenates the large list of thms with $args,*</p>",
        "id": 598429281,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780004900
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1030095\">Jannis</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Debug.20macro.20generating.20unsupportedSyntax.20exception/near/598428823\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>But why would I bind it at all in this example then? For only I somehow need to.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The only real reason is error reporting locations :)</p>\n<p>For example, consider the case where the nested <code>simp_all ...</code> reports an error on the <code>simp_all</code> token itself (red squiggle just to the end of the <code>_all</code>, not including the rest of the syntax).</p>\n<p>In the case where we just use <code>simp_all</code> and not <code>simp_all%$tk</code>, the error will wind up being reported on the position info of our synthetic <code>simp_all</code>, which is inferred just from the ambient syntax ref. The ambient syntax ref in this case is the whole syntax <code>custom_simp_all only [...]</code>, so the red squiggle will end up underneath the whole thing.</p>\n<p>But in the case where we use <code>custom_simp_all%$tk</code> and then <code>simp_all%$tk</code>, the synthetic <code>simp_all</code> now has the same position information as <code>custom_simp_all</code>. So an error reported on <code>simp_all</code> will now just put a red squiggle under the user-written <code>custom_simp_all</code> instead of <code>custom_simp_all only [...]</code>.</p>\n<p>So, no change to the logic, just a bit of polish and a good habit <span aria-label=\"grinning face with smiling eyes\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f601\" role=\"img\" title=\"grinning face with smiling eyes\">:grinning_face_with_smiling_eyes:</span>  Couldn't tell you if <code>simp_all</code> actually does report anything just on its initial token! <span aria-label=\"upside down\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f643\" role=\"img\" title=\"upside down\">:upside_down:</span></p>",
        "id": 598431514,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1780006032
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"custom_simp\"</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"s2\">\"only\"</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">dsimpArgs</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"custom_simp?\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"only\"</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">dsimpArgs</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">buildSimpArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TSepArray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"ss\">`Lean.Parser.Tactic.simpErase</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Lean.Parser.Tactic.simpLemma</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\",\"</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">MacroM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TSepArray</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"ss\">`Lean.Parser.Tactic.simpErase</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Lean.Parser.Tactic.simpLemma</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\",\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">baseArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">dsimpArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">thms</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">baseArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">baseArgs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TSepArray</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simpArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">none</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">baseArgs</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">elems</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">baseArgs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getElems</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getElems</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">TSepArray</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofElems</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">elems</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simpArgs</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">macro_rules</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">custom_simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"bp\">%$</span><span class=\"n\">onlyTk</span><span class=\"o\">]?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">]]?)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">buildSimpArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp_all</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"bp\">%$</span><span class=\"n\">onlyTk</span><span class=\"o\">]?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">custom_simp?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"bp\">%$</span><span class=\"n\">onlyTk</span><span class=\"o\">]?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">]]?)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">buildSimpArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp_all?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"bp\">%$</span><span class=\"n\">onlyTk</span><span class=\"o\">]?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>this is my solution.</p>",
        "id": 598431567,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780006055
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>the <code>.raw[1]...</code> part I'm not too sure about, but it works <span aria-label=\"man shrugging\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f937-200d-2642\" role=\"img\" title=\"man shrugging\">:man_shrugging:</span></p>",
        "id": 598431667,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780006109
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess the next cool thing would be for <code>custom_simp?</code> to only return the used theorems supplied by the user...</p>",
        "id": 598432732,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780006693
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But I have no idea how I would achieve that.</p>",
        "id": 598432743,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780006700
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, I don't think you're doing anything strictly <em>wrong</em> there, it would just be nice to find a way around that! XD <code>.raw[1]</code> isn't preferable, but the real code smell tbh is <code>TSepArray.mk</code>. Generally meta code should not be constructing typed syntax by hand, but every so often in a case like this you can't easily avoid it without introducing other code smells. Hmm...it would be nice to flesh out the TSepArray API and quotation machinery <span aria-label=\"thinking\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f914\" role=\"img\" title=\"thinking\">:thinking:</span></p>",
        "id": 598433068,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1780006920
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The thing is --- shouldn't dsimpArgs already give me something akin to like a TSepArray?</p>",
        "id": 598433193,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780007001
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I mean <code>args</code> in the macro rules already returns TSepArray. And that also uses dsimpArgs, no?</p>",
        "id": 598433254,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780007034
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think one way of getting that TSepArray would be to immediately match against the explicit <code>dsimpArgs</code> you construct, for instance with <code> `(dsimpArgs| [ $baseArgs,* ])</code>, then combine the <code>baseArgs</code> and <code>args</code> in another <code>dsimpArgs</code>. Though I'm not sure how the antiquotations work out...</p>\n<p>I wonder if theres a way to make your own parser for <code>(simpErase &lt;|&gt; simpLemma),*</code> which behaves nicely...</p>",
        "id": 598434042,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1780007457
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I tried</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">dsimpArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">baseArgs</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">])</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">dsimpArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">list</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">thms</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>but I get <code>non-exhaustive 'match' (syntax)</code>.</p>",
        "id": 598434355,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780007620
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, this is the trade-off: it is genuinely non-exhaustive, since syntax typing specifically is “fake”. So even though this <em>should</em> be exhaustive, there’s actually a fallback case that needs to be handled. If you use <code>let patt ← val | throwUnsupportedSyntax</code> it should work, but is of course also rather unfortunate.</p>",
        "id": 598462638,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1780022875
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Interesting. Probably still more idiomatic than what I was doing before.</p>",
        "id": 598488650,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780038029
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You ment <code>Macro.throwUnsupported</code> though, right? the other one doesn't work.</p>",
        "id": 598541382,
        "sender_full_name": "Jannis",
        "timestamp": 1780055466
    }
]